<title>JAPAN: Hitachi delays construction of Malaysia chip plant.</title>
<headline>Hitachi delays construction of Malaysia chip plant.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hitachi Ltd said on Friday that it would delay construction of a semiconductor factory planned in Kedah, Malaysia, because of sluggish semiconductor sales.</p>
<p>Hitachi and its South Korean semiconductor partner the LG group originally planned to start construction by the end of this year and begin production of 16 megabit and 64 megabit dynamic random access memory chips in early 1998.</p>
<p>&quot;The construction will be delayed, but Hitachi has not frozen the plan,&quot; a Hitachi spokesman said.</p>
<p>Hitachi did not say how long the delay might be.</p>
</text>
